  "change": [
    "The shared private send path retains one outgoing wire buffer and returns a borrow; individual message sends explicitly copy into their owned public return value.",
    "Reserved fanout computation uses the retained buffer instead of creating a returned ciphertext copy that the aggregate caller immediately discards.",
    "The fixed header reserves its exact size, and the send path reserves ciphertext plus tag together to avoid retaining geometric growth for the final tag."
  ],
  "retained_contracts": [
    "Same traffic cryptography, header bytes, message IDs, input/epoch/intent/capacity checks and persisted outbox representation.",
    "Same whole-batch reservation and whole-batch commit before public release; original per-member crash observation remains in the test-only boundary.",
    "Same private plaintext/AD ownership and zeroization; this change does not deduplicate retained per-recipient inputs or change storage format."
  ],
